A||||9||Alex4mula||Rebuild heads or whole engine?||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||01-30-2000||06:35 PM||||<BR>This is a Formula V6. Have diagnosed an oil leak in cyl. bad enough to missfire all time. Have a sticky valve in cyl. 3. I think the oil leak/missfire is valve related (guides). This developed slowly over +/- 2 years. I just need a temporary quick fix before investing in a new 3.4 with all the goodies. Should I take out the heads and rebuild them? How much that cost? How do I know for sure that the oil leak is through the valvetrain and not the cylinders rings (ie. engine rebuild)? Can I corroborate that taking the heads & inspecting the cyl. wall? What I want to avoid is to take out the engine now if posible and make it run ok. The engine has 70K miles since last rebuild. Thanks in advance for your advice.<BR>Alex4mula||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jim Baumann||01-30-2000||06:48 PM||||I have heard that if the car smokes only when it starts up you usually need a valve job. but if it smokes the whole time you are driving you usually need a ring job.  How was the problem diagnosed?||||reg||2
Z||000002||batboy||01-30-2000||07:37 PM||||Do a compression check of all the cylinders or at least the suspicious ones. Then do another check, but this time squirt some engine oil down the spark plug hole first. If the compression reading improves then there is ring wear. If it stays the same, the wear is mostly in the valves or guides. If the rings are good, then sure you can rebuild the heads without doing the rest. If the engine has high miles, I'd consider replacing the timing gears and chain too.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 01-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||01-30-2000||08:02 PM||||Fast fix and cheap.  Get an air hose nipple with spark plug threads, put the cylinder at tdc firing position and put in gear with emergency brake on to hold engine (valve covers off).  Put air pressure to the cylinder with air hose nipple, that holds the valves up.  Using a lever spring compressor remove the springs and put new valve seals (spring loaded viton) on and reinstall springs.  Do it six times and your stems should stay sealed until that 3.4 gets there.  I make it sound easy but I'm jealous about that 3.4!||||reg||1
Z||000004||la9||01-30-2000||08:08 PM||||If you take the heads to a machine shop you should have a little less than $200 to get them done. Ohio rates.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||01-30-2000||08:20 PM||||If you go ahead and get these heads built, why not "do it right"-port/polish/bowl blends etc. and use them on the 3.4 when you get it? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||01-30-2000||10:09 PM||||Thank you all for your inputs! It does not smoke while running but it does at startup. I'll do the test of putting oil in the spark plugs to make sure its a valve problem. If so then maybe I'll take them out to the shop. Thanks again for your help.<P>Alex4mula||||reg||12
Z||000007||WisconsinGT||01-30-2000||10:56 PM||||Alex,<P>I bought rebuilt heads about 6 months ago. Including the labor, it set me back $1,800. My back end is still sore. Anyway, I have a similar problem. Missfire on no.2 cylinder. Plus my car is using oil. I wonder if the heads are bad. Sounds like I need to check it out. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||mshill||01-31-2000||12:58 AM||||Just got my heads back from the shop this week.  They came off an 86SE with 190K original miles on it.  They charged me  the following for both heads: Standard valve grind (included complete teardown, magnaflux, and inspection) $60, Valve guides $50 plus $24 for parts, a couple of spring shims and two helicoils (for manifold bolts), and trimmed 0.050 for warpage $50.  They even cleaned all of the rocker arms and painted the exterior head surface at no cost.  Can't wait to get them on.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||01-31-2000||08:34 AM||||$1800??? Wow! I gess mechanics there are like here in FL. They charge like doctors. I will do all the work myself. Nobody touch my car. Too many bad experience$. Just need to find a machine shop for that part. This week will do final analysis. Hope it sure are the heads...||||reg||1
